lcos-updates (0.7-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cancel or close waits until the helper and its apt/dpkg children are gone
    before another check or install can start.
  * Helper install deadline kills the apt-get/dpkg process group before
    reporting the timeout.
  * Network and fetch failures, and install timeouts, are no longer shown as
    an update-check timeout.
  * GUI check budget covers the helper's apt-get update plus simulation.
  * A second launch raises the existing window. --check applies only to the
    launch that passed it.
  * Polkit asks to check for updates on simulate, and to install them on upgrade.
  * Project version 0.7.1 (About / meson). Debian package revision 0.7-2.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 18:09:19 +0000

